+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+Full-recall p95 of the `UserPromptSubmit` hook, measured on the adversarial
+synthetic 30-word vocabulary (`crates/muninn-bench`, Zipf-distributed
+vocabulary: 30 frequent domain words plus 2 000 rare identifiers):
+
+- **Before the term-selection fix: 10.27 ms p95.**
+- **Fix:** in `select_terms` (`crates/muninn-core/src/recall.rs`), drop prompt
+  terms whose document frequency `df` exceeds `n/3` (once the store has at
+  least 50 records) before scoring by IDF. A term that appears in more than a
+  third of the store carries no discriminative signal but still costs a long
+  posting-list scan, so excluding it from the top-k selection removes that
+  cost from the hot path.
+- **After the term-selection fix: 1.82 ms p95.**
+
+These numbers come from this project's own recorded measurements (bench runs
+observed in this project's transcripts); no other measured p95 for this
+specific scenario (adversarial 30-word vocabulary, full recall) was found
+committed in the repository, so no additional figures are reported here.
